<title>NORWAY: Norske Skog Q1 profits fall.</title>
<headline>Norske Skog Q1 profits fall.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to March 31</p>
<p>				(millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Operating revenue		    2,856    vs     3,448</p>
<p> Operating result			 170    vs	 654</p>
<p> - Fibre			     minus 27    vs  minus 45</p>
<p> - Paper				    198    vs	 690</p>
<p> - Building materials		    -5    vs  minus  1</p>
<p> Net financial items	     minus 52    vs  minus 84</p>
<p> Pre-tax result			   118    vs	 602</p>
<p> Result after tax			  85    vs	 429</p>
<p>NOTE -- Full name of Norway's largest forestry group is Norske Skogindustrier ASA. It had been expected to post a first-quarter pre-tax profit of 175 million crowns, according to seven analysts polled by Reuters.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
